    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Paul Gamiels Hill Lifesaving Station, built in 1878, once guarded Southern Shores while it was part of Kitty Hawk.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.outerbanks.com/southern-shores.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After a 1909 remodel, the station served both World Wars before being replaced, deserted, and finally burned in the 1960s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.outerbanks.com/southern-shores.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Visitors to Hillcrest Drive beach access find almost no trace of the historic lifesaving station that once stood there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.outerbanks.com/southern-shores.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Southern Shores sits in a hurricane‑prone zone, with the Atlantic season peaking from late August through September.",
